{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "version": "2026-11-15",
    "title": "peek",
    "description": "Keeps an agent's images, videos, audio, text and markdown where it made them, and serves them back by a link that plays or shows them in the browser, text up to 1 MB. **Agents** upload a file they made, a screenshot, a screen recording, a sound or a text or markdown report, saying what it is for (a repository and pull request, a waypoint task, tags), and give **the person** its `link`, which shows or plays it in their browser, on a phone too (text and markdown up to 1 MB show as text, markdown formatted).\n\n- **Upload** with `PutAsset`: the file's bytes are the request body, streamed to disk, so a several-GB video works. An agent with only the MCP server asks for an upload URL instead (`CreateUploadUrl`), and runs the `curl` it answers: the file never passes through the model, and the command needs no token.\n- **Find** with `ListAssets`, by repository, pull request, task, tags, media type, uploader or text, newest first.\n- **Serve:** an asset's `fileUrl` (`GetFile`) answers byte ranges, so a browser seeks a video; its `link` is the page that shows it.\n- **Change** what an asset is of with `UpdateAsset`, and remove it, file and all, with `DeleteAsset`.\n\n**Auth:** `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on everything but `GetHealth`, `PutUpload` (whose URL is its own single-use ticket), the docs and the page. Each token has a name, made with `peek token create <name>`; `PEEK_ADMIN_TOKEN` is one more, named `admin`. Every token may do everything. A browser signs in once with `CreateSession`, which sets a cookie that every call then takes, so `<img>`, `<video>` and `<audio>` load; a write signed in by the cookie alone must also send `x-peek: 1`, or is refused 403.\n\n**Uploader:** an asset's `createdBy` is the uploader's `x-actor` header, when it gives one, else its token's name.\n\n**Errors:** `{code, message}`, where `code` is an AWS-style exception name such as `ValidationException` or `ResourceNotFoundException`."
  },
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Assets",
      "description": "Upload, find, change and delete what peek keeps."
    },
    {
      "name": "Files",
      "description": "An asset's bytes, by its `fileUrl`."
    },
    {
      "name": "Sessions",
      "description": "Signing a browser in, so media elements load."
    },
    {
      "name": "Platform",
      "description": "Health."
    }
  ],
